  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The plane of polarized light is rotated by optically active compound, i.e. it should be chiral. \nSo, (A) has, chiral $\\mathrm{C-}$atom. So, it is optically active.\nIn (B), (C) and (D) plane of symmetry is present.\nHence, (A) is correct.",
